WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:03.039
of Scripture right here in the Gospel of Matthew.

00:00:03.039 --> 00:00:08.239
And the Gospels record much of the life and ministry of the Lord Jesus Christ.

00:00:08.239 --> 00:00:11.279
And I'm thankful that we have the Gospels.

00:00:11.279 --> 00:00:14.000
We understand that the life and ministry,

00:00:14.000 --> 00:00:18.879
especially the public ministry of the Lord Jesus Christ, is well documented.

00:00:18.879 --> 00:00:20.719
However, John would say it this way.

00:00:20.719 --> 00:00:24.559
I know I have you in Matthew chapter 8, John 21 and 25.

00:00:24.559 --> 00:00:25.600
The Bible says this,

00:00:25.680 --> 00:00:41.040
And what a great verse of Scripture that is.

00:00:41.040 --> 00:00:45.919
I've often meditated upon the truth of John 21-25

00:00:45.919 --> 00:00:50.560
and just all of the wonderful things that the disciples had the opportunity

00:00:50.560 --> 00:00:53.119
to be able to see and be eyewitnesses of.

00:00:53.119 --> 00:00:57.680
And we know that John there, the human penman of the Gospel of John,

00:00:57.680 --> 00:01:00.639
then also writing the epistles, 1st, 2nd, and 3rd John,

00:01:01.200 --> 00:01:05.760
specifically in the first letter, he mentions how he's an eyewitness

00:01:05.760 --> 00:01:07.760
and he's given this eyewitness account.

00:01:07.760 --> 00:01:10.080
And what a blessing that is.

00:01:10.080 --> 00:01:13.519
And we find that as you study through the Gospels,

00:01:13.519 --> 00:01:18.879
that we have an opportunity to see and to know exactly what God wants us to know.

00:01:18.879 --> 00:01:23.040
In His infinite wisdom, He chose to provide us with the accounts

00:01:23.040 --> 00:01:25.839
that are recorded here within the Scriptures.

00:01:25.839 --> 00:01:27.839
And we find that a number of times,

00:01:27.839 --> 00:01:31.919
that as we're going through these pages of Scripture,

00:01:32.800 --> 00:01:36.160
that we're told of those that are observing,

00:01:36.160 --> 00:01:41.279
those that are part of what's taking place in the life of the Lord Jesus Christ.

00:01:41.279 --> 00:01:44.319
The Bible will use this word, that they marveled.

00:01:44.319 --> 00:01:45.519
That they marveled.

00:01:45.519 --> 00:01:48.959
There's only a couple of occasions in which the Lord marveled,

00:01:48.959 --> 00:01:53.680
but we find there's a few more times in which the people marveled.

00:01:53.680 --> 00:01:57.279
And I was kind of just fixated upon that thought.

00:01:57.279 --> 00:01:59.519
And we'll look at a few passages this evening.

00:01:59.519 --> 00:02:03.680
And I've simply titled the message tonight, Marvel at Jesus.

00:02:04.239 --> 00:02:05.680
Marvel at Jesus.

00:02:05.680 --> 00:02:08.639
The word means to wonder exceedingly.

00:02:08.639 --> 00:02:13.119
It carries the idea of to be had in admiration.

00:02:13.679 --> 00:02:17.839
And Noah Webster said it this way in the 1828 Noah Webster's Dictionary,

00:02:17.839 --> 00:02:19.039
to define the word.

00:02:19.039 --> 00:02:20.320
He said, a wonder.

00:02:20.320 --> 00:02:22.080
But then I want you to listen to this carefully.

00:02:22.080 --> 00:02:25.520
It says, that which arrests the attention

00:02:27.759 --> 00:02:34.399
and causes a person to stand, gaze, or pause.

00:02:36.080 --> 00:02:37.360
Did you catch that this evening?

00:02:37.360 --> 00:02:40.720
So it's that which arrests the attention.

00:02:41.679 --> 00:02:42.399
You marvel.

00:02:43.520 --> 00:02:44.720
Something happens.

00:02:44.720 --> 00:02:46.720
Something is done.

00:02:46.720 --> 00:02:49.199
And we just stop.

00:02:49.199 --> 00:02:51.600
It catches our attention.

00:02:52.160 --> 00:02:54.240
It arrests our attention.

00:02:54.240 --> 00:02:58.000
It causes us to stand, gaze, or pause.

00:02:58.559 --> 00:03:02.080
As we look in the couple of chapters here in the book of Matthew,

00:03:02.080 --> 00:03:05.039
we'll look at three references within these two chapters.

00:03:05.039 --> 00:03:08.000
And look beginning in Matthew 8 and verse 23.

00:03:08.080 --> 00:03:11.039
Each of them are familiar portions of scripture,

00:03:11.039 --> 00:03:13.199
miracles that have taken place.

00:03:13.199 --> 00:03:16.800
And as we look at these, we'll find that in each of the passages,

00:03:16.800 --> 00:03:19.600
there's a reference to the people marveling.

00:03:20.639 --> 00:03:24.240
And we'll note what it is that caused them to marvel.

00:03:24.240 --> 00:03:26.240
The Bible says in verse 23 of Matthew 8,

00:03:26.240 --> 00:03:30.399
when he was entered into a ship, his disciples followed him.

00:03:30.399 --> 00:03:34.240
And behold, there arose a great tempest in the sea.

00:03:34.880 --> 00:03:37.600
In so much that the ship was covered with the waves,

00:03:37.679 --> 00:03:40.080
but he was asleep.

00:03:41.520 --> 00:03:43.919
His disciples came to him and awoke him saying,

00:03:43.919 --> 00:03:45.600
Lord, save us.

00:03:46.399 --> 00:03:47.119
We perish.

00:03:48.000 --> 00:03:52.320
I believe that they had a lot more urgency than what I just read it as.

00:03:52.320 --> 00:03:55.279
I think that they probably came there and they said,

00:03:55.279 --> 00:03:56.639
Lord, save us.

00:03:56.639 --> 00:03:57.520
We perish.

00:03:57.520 --> 00:04:00.559
I mean, they're anxious about the circumstances,

00:04:00.559 --> 00:04:03.360
the situation that they find themselves in.

00:04:03.440 --> 00:04:06.160
And Jesus says to them in verse 26,

00:04:06.160 --> 00:04:10.160
why are ye fearful, O ye of little faith?

00:04:10.800 --> 00:04:14.880
Then he arose and rebuked the winds and the sea,

00:04:14.880 --> 00:04:16.480
and there was a great calm.

00:04:16.480 --> 00:04:19.279
Now I know that we're familiar with this passage of scripture.

00:04:19.920 --> 00:04:23.200
In fact, some of us have read through this passage of scripture

00:04:23.200 --> 00:04:25.440
and we just keep on reading right through it

00:04:25.440 --> 00:04:30.880
because the account of Jesus calming the storm is familiar to us.

00:04:31.440 --> 00:04:33.440
We've heard it time and again,

00:04:33.440 --> 00:04:36.239
but I want you to notice that on this particular day,

00:04:36.239 --> 00:04:37.920
in this particular setting,

00:04:37.920 --> 00:04:39.679
the Bible says in verse 27,

00:04:39.679 --> 00:04:42.160
but the men marveled.

00:04:43.359 --> 00:04:44.160
They marveled.

00:04:44.880 --> 00:04:46.000
And here's what they said.

00:04:46.000 --> 00:04:53.679
What manner of man is this that even the winds and the sea obey him?

00:04:54.399 --> 00:04:57.200
As we get to think about this particular reference

00:04:57.200 --> 00:04:59.279
in the gospel of Matthew with the people,

00:04:59.279 --> 00:05:01.200
the disciples specifically,

00:05:01.200 --> 00:05:03.040
where it says that they marveled,

00:05:04.079 --> 00:05:07.279
it was because of his power over nature.

00:05:08.239 --> 00:05:10.480
The fact that he could stand and say,

00:05:10.480 --> 00:05:11.600
peace, be still,

00:05:12.160 --> 00:05:15.119
in the midst of a storm that caused these disciples

00:05:15.119 --> 00:05:18.160
who were familiar with being on the Sea of Galilee

00:05:18.160 --> 00:05:20.000
to fear for their very lives.

00:05:21.040 --> 00:05:23.200
And he just stood and he said,

00:05:23.839 --> 00:05:25.359
peace, be still.

00:05:26.079 --> 00:05:27.040
And he rebuked.

00:05:27.040 --> 00:05:31.200
Here it says that he rebuked the wind and the sea,

00:05:31.200 --> 00:05:32.399
and there was a great calm.

00:05:32.959 --> 00:05:34.640
And it says that they marveled.

00:05:35.760 --> 00:05:38.000
In chapter number nine, in verse number one,

00:05:39.440 --> 00:05:41.119
the Bible says that he entered into a ship

00:05:41.119 --> 00:05:43.279
and passed over and came into his own city.

00:05:44.239 --> 00:05:47.279
And behold, they brought to him a man sick of the palsy,

00:05:47.279 --> 00:05:48.079
laying on a bed.

00:05:48.079 --> 00:05:49.600
And Jesus, seeing their faith,

00:05:49.600 --> 00:05:51.839
said unto the sick of the palsy,

00:05:51.839 --> 00:05:53.200
son, be of good cheer,

00:05:53.200 --> 00:05:56.079
thy sins be forgiven thee.

00:05:56.079 --> 00:05:58.000
Now, Mark gives us in chapter number two,

00:05:58.000 --> 00:05:59.119
a little bit more detail

00:05:59.119 --> 00:06:00.720
with regard to this particular miracle.

00:06:00.720 --> 00:06:02.559
This is the man that's born of four.

00:06:02.559 --> 00:06:03.679
Remember, there's so many people

00:06:03.679 --> 00:06:04.799
that are thronged at the house,

00:06:04.799 --> 00:06:05.679
there's no way in,

00:06:05.679 --> 00:06:07.040
and they go up on the rooftop

00:06:07.040 --> 00:06:09.279
and they move the tiles and they let them down.

00:06:09.279 --> 00:06:11.519
And that whole scene, that's Mark chapter two.

00:06:12.079 --> 00:06:14.320
This is Matthew's account of that.

00:06:14.320 --> 00:06:16.959
And Jesus says, be of good cheer,

00:06:16.959 --> 00:06:18.640
thy sins be forgiven thee.

00:06:18.640 --> 00:06:19.679
And behold, verse three,

00:06:19.679 --> 00:06:22.160
certain of the scribes said within themselves,

00:06:22.160 --> 00:06:23.679
this man blasphemeth.

00:06:23.679 --> 00:06:24.799
Notice it says this,

00:06:24.799 --> 00:06:27.279
and Jesus, knowing their thoughts,

00:06:27.279 --> 00:06:29.519
I preached about that a little bit this morning,

00:06:29.519 --> 00:06:32.160
and he knows our thoughts, amen.

00:06:32.160 --> 00:06:33.519
And notice what he said,

00:06:33.519 --> 00:06:36.720
wherefore think ye evil in your hearts.

00:06:36.720 --> 00:06:39.279
Now, they rightly understood

00:06:39.279 --> 00:06:42.399
that who can forgive sins but God only.

00:06:42.399 --> 00:06:43.920
Mark references that,

00:06:43.920 --> 00:06:46.079
that's a proper conclusion.

00:06:46.079 --> 00:06:48.720
The problem that these onlookers had,

00:06:48.720 --> 00:06:50.399
these religious leaders,

00:06:50.399 --> 00:06:52.640
is that they didn't believe Jesus was God.

00:06:53.440 --> 00:06:55.279
And so they had real issue

00:06:55.279 --> 00:06:57.760
with the fact that only God can forgive sin,

00:06:57.760 --> 00:07:00.880
but Jesus said, thy sins be forgiven.

00:07:00.880 --> 00:07:03.359
And so they were really confused

00:07:03.359 --> 00:07:04.239
and they're thinking

00:07:04.239 --> 00:07:05.440
and they're having these thoughts.

00:07:05.440 --> 00:07:08.880
And here it says that they charge him with blasphemy.

00:07:09.920 --> 00:07:11.760
Notice in verse number five,

00:07:11.760 --> 00:07:14.559
for whether it is easier to say,

00:07:14.559 --> 00:07:16.399
thy sins be forgiven thee,

00:07:16.399 --> 00:07:18.480
or to say arise and walk,

00:07:18.480 --> 00:07:21.200
but that ye may know that the son of man

00:07:21.200 --> 00:07:24.399
hath power on earth to forgive sins.

00:07:24.399 --> 00:07:26.720
So he makes that statement in verse number six,

00:07:26.720 --> 00:07:27.760
the beginning part,

00:07:27.760 --> 00:07:29.279
to those religious leaders,

00:07:29.279 --> 00:07:32.079
those scribes that were saying within themselves

00:07:32.079 --> 00:07:34.079
that Jesus blasphemeth.

00:07:34.079 --> 00:07:35.920
We find that he says to them,

00:07:35.920 --> 00:07:37.839
that ye may know that the son of man

00:07:37.839 --> 00:07:39.920
hath power on earth to forgive sins.

00:07:39.920 --> 00:07:41.760
Then you look at that parenthesis there,

00:07:41.760 --> 00:07:43.600
then saith he to the sick of the palsy.

00:07:43.600 --> 00:07:45.200
So he directs his attention

00:07:45.200 --> 00:07:47.040
to the sick man that was brought in,

00:07:47.040 --> 00:07:51.040
born afore, arise, take up thy bed,

00:07:51.119 --> 00:07:54.160
and go unto thine house.

00:07:55.760 --> 00:07:57.279
But then the next words say,

00:07:57.279 --> 00:08:00.880
and he arose and departed to his house.

00:08:01.839 --> 00:08:03.519
But when the multitude saw it,

00:08:03.519 --> 00:08:04.480
notice what it says,

00:08:04.480 --> 00:08:08.559
they marveled and glorified God,

00:08:08.559 --> 00:08:12.320
which had given such power unto men.

00:08:12.320 --> 00:08:13.600
You don't have to turn there,

00:08:13.600 --> 00:08:17.119
but Mark's account ends it in verse number 12

00:08:17.119 --> 00:08:18.239
by saying this,

00:08:18.959 --> 00:08:22.239
we never saw it on this fashion.

00:08:22.799 --> 00:08:24.399
This was something that was,

00:08:24.399 --> 00:08:25.839
they'd never witnessed this,

00:08:25.839 --> 00:08:27.359
they never experienced this,

00:08:27.359 --> 00:08:29.040
this man that comes in,

00:08:29.040 --> 00:08:30.320
that's born afore,

00:08:30.320 --> 00:08:32.479
this man that's sick of the palsy,

00:08:32.479 --> 00:08:34.799
he's paralyzed and he's carried in.

00:08:34.799 --> 00:08:35.760
And Jesus says,

00:08:35.760 --> 00:08:37.679
thy sins be forgiven thee.

00:08:37.679 --> 00:08:39.919
And there's that interaction once again

00:08:39.919 --> 00:08:42.719
where Jesus proves his deity

00:08:42.719 --> 00:08:45.440
and he proves it by showing his power

00:08:45.840 --> 00:08:46.640
to not,

00:08:46.640 --> 00:08:48.080
his power to forgive sin

00:08:48.080 --> 00:08:50.719
is really the impact of this passage

00:08:50.719 --> 00:08:52.799
or the main focus of this passage.

00:08:52.799 --> 00:08:54.159
But he says to that man,

00:08:54.159 --> 00:08:59.119
take up thy bed and go unto thine house.

00:08:59.679 --> 00:09:00.960
Now the reality is that

00:09:00.960 --> 00:09:02.640
any of us could say those words,

00:09:03.359 --> 00:09:04.960
but none of us have that power.

00:09:06.400 --> 00:09:06.900
Amen?

00:09:07.599 --> 00:09:08.479
We could say it,

00:09:09.520 --> 00:09:11.440
but all the while he'd still lay there.

00:09:13.280 --> 00:09:14.479
And it says he arose

00:09:15.119 --> 00:09:16.640
and departed to his house.

00:09:16.640 --> 00:09:17.919
And notice the impact,

00:09:17.919 --> 00:09:19.359
it says that there were multitudes.

00:09:19.359 --> 00:09:20.080
Now again,

00:09:20.080 --> 00:09:21.599
I referenced Mark's gospel

00:09:21.599 --> 00:09:22.799
because Mark says

00:09:22.799 --> 00:09:24.000
that there's so many people,

00:09:24.000 --> 00:09:25.119
they can't get to the house.

00:09:25.119 --> 00:09:26.719
I mean, that's how many people are there

00:09:26.719 --> 00:09:28.239
listening to Jesus teach.

00:09:28.239 --> 00:09:31.200
So all of these people see this

00:09:31.200 --> 00:09:32.799
and the Bible says the multitudes,

00:09:32.799 --> 00:09:34.239
they marveled.

00:09:34.239 --> 00:09:35.200
Now remember,

00:09:35.200 --> 00:09:37.440
as we think about that word marvel,

00:09:37.440 --> 00:09:40.000
it means that which arrests the attention.

00:09:40.000 --> 00:09:40.960
Do you not think

00:09:40.960 --> 00:09:42.719
that would arrest the attention?

00:09:42.719 --> 00:09:43.599
Do you not think

00:09:43.599 --> 00:09:45.119
that would cause someone

00:09:45.119 --> 00:09:47.280
to stand, gaze, or pause

00:09:47.280 --> 00:09:48.799
because they've seen something

00:09:48.799 --> 00:09:50.719
that they've never seen before?

00:09:50.719 --> 00:09:52.159
They've witnessed something,

00:09:52.159 --> 00:09:54.080
they've experienced something

00:09:54.080 --> 00:09:56.080
that they've never experienced before.

00:09:56.880 --> 00:09:58.799
And the Bible says they marveled.

00:09:58.799 --> 00:09:59.919
Continue in Matthew chapter...

00:09:59.919 --> 00:10:03.479
In Matthew 9, if you will, look at verse 32.

00:10:03.479 --> 00:10:08.459
In Matthew 9 and verse 32, the Bible says,

00:10:08.459 --> 00:10:13.459
As they went out, behold, they brought to him a dumb man

00:10:13.459 --> 00:10:17.299
possessed with a devil.

00:10:17.299 --> 00:10:20.599
And when the devil was cast out, the dumb spake.

00:10:20.599 --> 00:10:22.839
And the multitudes... what's it say?

00:10:22.839 --> 00:10:24.739
They marveled.

00:10:24.739 --> 00:10:27.139
The multitudes marveled, saying,

00:10:27.139 --> 00:10:33.039
He was never so seen in Israel.

00:10:33.039 --> 00:10:36.879
These are three references within just really

00:10:36.879 --> 00:10:39.719
a small portion of the Gospels,

00:10:39.719 --> 00:10:43.519
just part of Matthew 8, part of Matthew 9.

00:10:43.519 --> 00:10:47.359
And we see here the focus of Matthew 9, 32, and 33.

00:10:47.359 --> 00:10:49.999
They marveled at his power to heal,

00:10:49.999 --> 00:10:51.359
to cast out demons.

00:10:51.359 --> 00:10:55.499
See, listen, our Lord has power over nature.

00:10:55.499 --> 00:10:57.099
He has power over sin.

00:10:57.099 --> 00:10:59.159
He has power over devils.

00:10:59.159 --> 00:11:01.699
He has power over sickness and disease.

00:11:01.699 --> 00:11:03.299
He has all power.

00:11:03.299 --> 00:11:06.139
And we find that he demonstrated his power

00:11:06.139 --> 00:11:07.539
through these miracles.

00:11:07.539 --> 00:11:09.839
And on these specific accounts

00:11:09.839 --> 00:11:11.679
that we've looked at this evening,

00:11:11.679 --> 00:11:15.019
the impact on the people that are there,

00:11:15.019 --> 00:11:16.619
the first being the disciples,

00:11:16.619 --> 00:11:19.479
but then multitudes in the next two accounts,

00:11:19.479 --> 00:11:23.219
the Bible says that they marveled.

00:11:23.219 --> 00:11:25.259
I think about the words not used there,

00:11:26.019 --> 00:11:26.859
but in Acts chapter number one,

00:11:26.859 --> 00:11:28.419
in verses 10 and 11,

00:11:28.419 --> 00:11:29.979
after the Lord Jesus Christ

00:11:29.979 --> 00:11:31.979
had gone to the cross of Calvary,

00:11:31.979 --> 00:11:33.839
he was buried in a borrowed tomb.

00:11:33.839 --> 00:11:36.279
He rose conquering sin, death, and the grave.

00:11:36.279 --> 00:11:38.099
He's given instruction.

00:11:38.099 --> 00:11:39.579
He's walked there upon the earth

00:11:39.579 --> 00:11:41.279
after his resurrection,

00:11:41.279 --> 00:11:43.219
provided instruction for these days,

00:11:43.219 --> 00:11:46.099
and now he's going to ascend to heaven.

00:11:47.379 --> 00:11:49.139
And I want you to notice that

00:11:49.139 --> 00:11:50.739
within the text of Scripture

00:11:50.739 --> 00:11:52.219
that we so often look to

00:11:52.219 --> 00:11:56.299
and understand the fact of the ascension,

00:11:56.299 --> 00:11:58.579
the Bible says in verse number 10,

00:11:58.579 --> 00:12:02.059
and while they look steadfastly toward heaven

00:12:02.059 --> 00:12:02.899
as he went up,

00:12:02.899 --> 00:12:04.079
why'd they do that?

00:12:04.079 --> 00:12:05.179
Because they marveled.

00:12:07.019 --> 00:12:08.459
Because they marveled.

00:12:08.459 --> 00:12:10.179
The Bible says that behold,

00:12:10.179 --> 00:12:11.699
two men stood by them in white apparel,

00:12:11.699 --> 00:12:13.179
which also said, you men of Galilee,

00:12:13.179 --> 00:12:14.219
notice what they say,

00:12:14.219 --> 00:12:17.019
why stand ye gazing up into heaven?

00:12:17.019 --> 00:12:17.899
Remember the word,

00:12:17.899 --> 00:12:19.619
it means that which arrests the attention

00:12:19.619 --> 00:12:21.099
and causes a person to stand,

00:12:21.099 --> 00:12:23.059
gaze or pause.

00:12:23.059 --> 00:12:25.459
Why stand ye gazing up into heaven?

00:12:25.459 --> 00:12:27.019
Because we've just seen something

00:12:27.019 --> 00:12:28.939
that we've never seen before.

00:12:28.939 --> 00:12:30.659
Because we've just experienced something

00:12:30.659 --> 00:12:32.699
that we've never experienced before,

